# 69. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT DIRECTIVE

**BUILD THE FUNCTIONAL SYSTEM, NOT JUST THE INTERFACE.**

Do not implement fake buttons, simulated operations, placeholder responses, or AI messages that claim to have modified content without actually modifying the underlying document.

Every advertised operation must connect to an executable application function.

Every successful operation must update the authoritative document model.

Every affected component must synchronize.

Every substantial operation must be recoverable.

Every generated PDF must be validated to the extent supported by the available infrastructure.

Do not remove existing working functionality.

Do not sacrifice source-content integrity for convenience.

Do not silently discard user content.

Do not silently resolve substantive conflicts.

Do not claim an operation was completed unless the actual document state confirms it.

If a feature requires an external service or integration, identify the dependency and provide an integration status rather than pretending it works.

